desc:TwoStorms Saturator
//tags: distortion saturation multiband
//author: TwoStorms
//version: 1.0
//
// A multiband saturator with an Act built in: its output gain, meters, Auto (Target, Match, Reference),
// Drive link and Finale are a TwoStorms Act, so TwoStorms Gain Stage lists and stages it like one.
// Up to six bands (Linkwitz-Riley crossovers at 12, 24 or 48 dB/oct, phase-compensated so the bands sum flat),
// each with one of 30 distortion styles (tubes, tapes, transformers, amps, console, fuzz, folds, bit crush...),
// Drive, Mix, Level, Dynamics (gate to compress), Feedback with its own frequency, Bass / Mid / Treble /
// Presence tone, drive and level balance, and Stereo or Mid/Side processing. Optional 2x / 4x oversampling.
// Eight modulation slots (tempo-synced LFO, envelope follower with sidechain, MIDI) can move any band control.
// Input gain, global drive, dynamics and mix, solo and mute per band, delta, A/B sets with level-matched Bypass and Swap,
// and an analyzer with draggable crossovers and band drive.
// Needs REAPER 6.74 or newer.
slider1:0<0,3,1{2,4,6,8}>-Channels
slider2:0<0,2,1{Auto,Always,Never}>-Finale (Auto = the last Act in the chain)
